## 📄 5. THE SQL FILE — `database/sql/full_schema_and_queries.sql`

This file is the source of truth. It must contain, in this order:

1. `CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS coaching_management CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci; USE coaching_management;`
2. `DROP TABLE IF EXISTS` in reverse FK order
3. `CREATE TABLE` for all 20+ tables with FK, unique, index, soft-delete (`deleted_at`)
4. `CREATE INDEX` for hot columns (phone, batch_id, attendance_date, fee_status)
5. `INSERT` seed data:
   - 1 Super Admin (bcrypt-hashed password — document in README)
   - Roles: Super Admin, Teacher, Accountant, Receptionist, Student, Parent
   - Permission codes for every module/action
   - `system_menus` default rows (Dashboard, Staff, Courses, Batches, Students, Fees, Attendance, Tests, Expenses, Reports, Notifications, Roles, Menus, Settings, Audit)
   - Default `settings`, `notification_templates`
6. `SELECT` queries for every list view (joins, filters, pagination)
7. `INSERT` / `UPDATE` / `DELETE` example queries for every CRUD action
8. Aggregate queries (revenue, defaulters, weak students, teacher attendance)
9. Recursive menu tree (`WITH RECURSIVE`)
10. Audit trail query

**Every Eloquent call in the app must have a matching raw SQL here.** Header comment must explain execution order.

