## 🔑 6. ADVANCED FEATURES & INPUT LOGIC

### 6.1 Dynamic Sidebar (Critical)

**Schema:** `system_menus(id, parent_id, name, icon, route_name, url, sort_order, is_visible, permission_code, created_by, updated_by, timestamps)`

**`SidebarComposer.php`:**
```php
public function compose(View $view) {
    $user = auth()->user();
    $cacheKey = 'sidebar_'.$user->id.'_'.md5($user->getAllPermissions()->pluck('name')->implode(','));
    $menus = Cache::remember($cacheKey, 3600, function () use ($user) {
        return SystemMenu::where('is_visible', 1)
            ->when($user->hasRole('super-admin') === false, function ($q) use ($user) {
                $q->whereIn('permission_code', $user->getAllPermissions()->pluck('name'));
            })
            ->orderBy('sort_order')
            ->get()
            ->toTree();  // custom method: group by parent_id
    });
    $view->with('sidebarMenus', $menus);
}
```

**Blade `components/sidebar.blade.php`:**
```blade
<aside class="main-sidebar">
  @foreach($sidebarMenus as $menu)
    @include('components.sidebar-item', ['menu' => $menu])
  @endforeach
</aside>
```

**Menu Builder UI** (`/admin/menus`): drag-drop sortable (SortableJS via `resources/js/admin.js`), fields — name, icon, route_name, url, parent, sort_order, permission_code, is_visible.

**Cache invalidation:** `MenuService::clearCache()` called in store/update/delete → flushes all `sidebar_*` keys.

